454	/// `live_secrets`: known-credential values (see
455	/// [`callisto_model::known_credential_env_values`]) to redact from each
456	/// line *before* it's echoed live to the terminal via `eprintln!`. This is
457	/// deliberately separate from -- and does not affect -- the `captured`
458	/// buffer that becomes the returned `CommandOutput.stderr`: that copy must
459	/// stay byte-for-byte raw so downstream classifiers (e.g.
460	/// `extract_retry_after_duration`, `detect_auth_failure`) can still match
461	/// exact upstream text. Callers pass the secrets list in rather than this
462	/// function reading the environment itself, keeping it pure and testable
